  "atmosSubject": "weatherx-hq/atmos master merge of PR #505 (a failed HRRR or AIFS collector abstains from the whole release), 2026-10-08 UTC. Moving from e5fd5758aab079c32c6b077857e641ba40970d04 spans five first-parent merges: #502, #499, #504, #503, #505. Under data/, ops/ and requirements* 18 files changed: PR #505 ops/core_model_artifact.py, ops/test_core_model_artifact.py and a data/bake.sh comment plus a legacy-path removal of app/public/data/core-model-roster.json (install() now reads CORE_COLLECTOR_RESULTS: ECMWF+GFS required; a failed HRRR is carried at most 10 h at install for the 12 h release gate, AIFS at most 24 h; the roster records it carried); PR #502 ops/fusion/{ci_collect.py, fusion_eval_common.py, fusion_eval_protocol.v3_2.json, model_point_capture.py, reference_collector.py, run_study.py} with tests and ops/test_ci_efficiency.py; PR #504 data/build_commercial_gfs_temperature.py, ops/commercial/publish-source.mjs and their tests; PR #503 ops/commercial/sandbox-journey.mjs; PR #499 none. Only the #505 files are executed by a pinned lane (data/bake.sh and ops/core_model_artifact.py in the whole bake); ops/fusion/** and ops/commercial/** are not imported or run by ops/bake-weatherx.sh, ops/platform/* or any workflow that reads this declaration (checked with git grep). The five observation producers, data/observation_freshness.py, data/requirements.txt, data/requirements.lock, ops/platform/publish-r2-component.sh, ops/bake-weatherx.sh, ops/bake-observation-points.sh and ops/weather-lab-ready.sh are byte-identical. Outside data/ and ops/, 23 app/ files changed, all from PR #499 (app/src chrome, cmdk, flights, i18n catalogs, routecard, test, voyage; app/scripts; app/e2e/journeys); app/package.json and app/package-lock.json are unchanged, so npm ci --prefix app installs the same tree, but the app/src changes reach the whole bake's blocking npx vite build. Previous pin e5fd5758a was the master merge of PR #501 (GFS point tail banded read) on top of #492. Atmos CI (ci run 37709913566, quality run 37709913568) was still running at this SHA when the pin moved; a passing whole bake at this pin is unverified until one runs.",
